The code comes from the tag swift-6.4.0-RELEASE at commit
1c9871b3a0c96232d3a4db8399913198395c4303. These directories hold it.

  Sources/CCompletionScoring
  Sources/CompletionScoring
  Sources/CompletionScoringTestSupport
  Tests/CompletionScoringTests
  Tests/CompletionScoringPerfTests

The following changes were made to the original. Each changed file carries a
notice below its license header.

- Declarations of the CompletionScoring module that had package access are
  public. Its extensions of standard library types and its binary
  serialization keep package access. The serialization is BinaryCodable,
  BinaryEncoder, BinaryDecoder, and the members that implement BinaryCodable.
- Public types whose stored properties are all Sendable declare the Sendable
  conformance that the compiler inferred for them at package access.
- The test support no longer imports the SwiftExtensions and
  ToolsProtocolsSwiftExtensions modules of sourcekit-lsp.
  Sources/CompletionScoringTestSupport/StandaloneSupport.swift defines the two
  helpers that it took from them, and a resource check calls
  FileManager.fileExists(atPath:).
- Tests/CompletionScoringTests/CompletionScoreTests.swift imports
  CompletionScoring publicly because its extensions declare public members.
- The CMake files are removed. Package.swift builds the modules with SwiftPM.
